<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of National Defence</h1><p class="st-meta">1916 CE – 1917 CE · capital Thessaloniki</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rival Greek government set up in Thessaloniki in 1916 by Eleftherios Venizelos, which took Greece into the First World War on the Allied side.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i-of-greece">King Constantine I</a> insisted on neutrality while Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a> wanted to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/triple-entente">Entente</a>. After Venizelos was forced out, officers in Allied-held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessaloniki</a> launched the National Defence movement in August 1916. In September and October Venizelos formed a provisional government there with Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlos-kountouriotis">Pavlos Kountouriotis</a> and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panagiotis-danglis">Panagiotis Danglis</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government, led by this triumvirate, controlled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> and most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands with Allied support, raised an army and declared war on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Greece was split in two, the National Schism, while Allied pressure on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> led to the armed clash of December 1916, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noemvriana">Noemvriana</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In June 1917 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a> to leave the country. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Venizelos</a> returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> as prime minister of a united <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece</a>, which entered the war fully. The bitterness of the schism shaped Greek politics for decades.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-national-defence.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of National Defence" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: (of code) User:Makaristos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Greece_(1822-1978).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1916 CE – 1917 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thessaloniki</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Eleftherios Venizelos, Pavlos Kountouriotis, Panagiotis Danglis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Government of National Defence, Thessaloniki government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1916&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-national-defence" aria-label="Provisional Government of National Defence on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5242 726 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of National Defence lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5562 982L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5562 982h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5562 982h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thessaloniki. <a href="/atlas?year=1916&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-national-defence">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
